          "bodyExcerpt": "Wampler Pedals Tumnus Germanium Deluxe | Effects Database Skip to navigation Brands &#9660; 0-9... a... b... c... d... e... f... g... h... i... j... k... l... m... n... o... p... q... r... s... t... u... v... w... x... y... z... Effect types &#9660; boost distortion fuzz overdrive acoustic simulation amp simulation speaker/cabinet simulation chorus flanger phaser tremolo vibe vibrato other modulation pitch shifter octaver delay reverb looper/sampler hold/freeze eq filter wah fuzz-wah bitcrusher ring modulator samplerate reducer wavefolder synth effect granular effect multi effect vocal effect talkbox vocoder buffer compressor other... Countries &#9660; (country unknown) Argentina Australia Austria Belarus Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Costa Rica Croatia Czech Republic Czechoslovakia DDR Denmark Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt Estonia Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Iran Ireland Israel Italy Japan Latvia Lithuania Luxembourg Macedonia Malaysia Malta Mexico Moldova Monaco Morocco Netherlands New-Zealand Norway Panama Peru Philippines Poland Portugal Romania Russia Serbia Singapore Slovakia Slovenia South-Africa South-Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Turkey U.K. U.S.A. U.S.S.R. Ukraine Uruguay Venezuela Browse by &#9660; Enclosure type Modulation type Special &#9658; Classics Eye candy Funny Vaporware Weird Random brand Random effect Events &#9658; NAMM Musikmesse Music China Guitar Summit More... &#9660; Forum (opens in new tab) myFXDB (opens in new tab) Newsletter About How to get listed? Interviews Reviews Effects explained Books D.I.Y. Schematics Links Contact Install Effects Database App Search the database browse by brand I... IndyGuitarist Wampler Pedals browse by type distortion/fuzz/overdrive overdrive browse by enclosure pedal Wampler Pedals Tumnus Germanium Deluxe Published on March 3, 2025 Wampler Pedals overdrive pedal Information Wampler Pedals The Germanium Tumnus Deluxe adds vintage sizzle and extra bite to a classic pedal, with increased options for gain switching, three band EQ, and switchable buffer. \"This is my shot at the ultimate Klon-style overdrive…​\" Legendary Diodes, Iconic Tone There are so many Klones out there that it's hard to keep up. That's just fine with me. My original Tumnus is still a favorite of guitarists around the world. That said, they're nearly all missing the unique germanium diodes that powered Bill Finnegan's classic design. Not so with the Germanium Tumnus Deluxe. I found an exceedingly rare stash of germanium diodes electronically identical to the ones Finnegan used. Thanks to them, the Germanium Tumnus Deluxe is as close as you can get to his '90s icons. That Tone With Any Rig, Every Time The Germanium Tumnus Deluxe and the sold-out Germanium Tumnus are essentially the same circuits. The Deluxe's 3-band EQ just gives you finer control without losing the pedal's inherent character. Want to add a bit of low-end back into the mix? Need some extra cut and attack? How about boosting a crunchy amp with a tighter, more percussive sound? It's all there, and it's all authentic. More Gain With the Flip of a Switch The Germanium Tumnus Deluxe also features my \"hot switch,\" which introduces more output and drive than most Klones. That includes my my OG Tumnus. This style of pedal is already a quintessential clean boost and mid-gain overdrive. Now, it has a meaner side while retaining the classic vocal-like tone and throaty response you expect. To Buffer or Not to Buffer This style of overdrive pedal gives your tone more clarity and character. It's often used as an always-on tonal sweetener but still adds some magic when bypassed. Still, there are plenty of us who want our pedals entirely out of the way when not in use. That's why I gave the Germanium Tumnus Deluxe a side-mounted buffer-bypass toggle switch. Keep it on for a bit of sparkle, or flip it off for an unadulterated signal path. Your choice. Technical Details Built in the U.S.A",
