          "title": "Golden Jubilee | Wampler Pedals",
          "h1": "Golden Jubilee",
          "description": "The Golden Jubilee is Brian Wampler&#039;s take on those fire-breathing amps that defined the sound of the 1980s. This pedal captures the thick, harmonically rich tones of American boutique amps and combines them with the raw, aggressive power of British high-gain monsters.",
          "snippet": "Golden Jubilee - Wampler Pedals",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Golden Jubilee | Wampler Pedals Home Shop All Pedals Distortion / Overdrive Compression Fuzz Delay / Reverb Modulation Boost Utilities Discontinued Plugins Merchandise Dealers Community Blog Artists Podcast Videos Support About Downloads FAQs Warranty Registration Withdrawal Request Contact Us search account_circle My Account search Products search Golden Jubilee A Celebration of Iconic British and American Amp Tones. In stock Golden Jubilee quantity Add to cart Watch video Overview Features Videos Technical Downloads In stock Golden Jubilee quantity Add to cart &#8220;The Golden Jubilee fuses my favorite British and American amp tones into one pedal&#8221; Right facing | Front | Left facing | Back | Top |' data-navmenu=\"off\" data-hashurl=\"off\" data-menuSlider=\"off\" data-continue-autoplay=\"off\" data-outside-nav=\"off\" data-autoplay=\"off\" > 4 5 A Milestone in Tone The Golden Jubilee is Brian Wampler's take on those fire-breathing amps that defined the sound of the 1980s. This pedal captures the thick, harmonically rich tones of American boutique amps and combines them with the raw, aggressive power of British high-gain monsters. It's compact enough to fit on any pedalboard, but when you plug in, it delivers the presence of a full stack - without the herniated disc from hauling it around. This is a workhorse pedal built to survive the real world and keep delivering night after night. It's your complete gain solution: crushing rhythm tones, singing leads, and that extra boost for solos - all in one pedal. No complicated switching or tap-dancing required. The gold-anodized controls against that emerald green sparkle finish aren't just for looks - they're a statement that this pedal is as bold as it sounds. Real amp tones and feel, crafted with precision At its core the Golden Jubilee is a celebration of severely awesome guitar tones. What began as a personal milestone evolved into a defining piece of the Wampler story. It captures the essence of two classic amplifier styles from the annals of musical history - and hands you total control over both. This pedal is for players chasing a palette of signature gain tones with character that feels alive and inspired. As with every Wampler pedal, The Golden Jubilee is built in the U.S.A. using only the highest-quality components. Every detail has been designed to ensure superior sound, reliability, and performance. &#36; 239.97 In stock Golden Jubilee quantity Add to cart SKU: WMP-GJB-PED Category: Distortion / Overdrive Tags: distortion , overdrive warning Cancer and Reproductive Harm www.p65warnings.ca.gov Two Legends, One Box The Distortion (DS) channel captures the smooth, articulate punch of those mid 80s high-end California boutique amps, keeping your notes clear even when you’re running heavy gain. It responds fast to your bends and phrasing, and gets you into pinch-harmonic territory without any fight. The Overdrive (OD) channel delivers that saturated, muscular British crunch that’s all over the records you love. It’s built to bloom into rich harmonics and absolutely crushes rhythm work, giving you that tight, percussive chug that players are always chasing when they’re hammering out palm-muted riffs. Stack both channels together and the Golden Jubilee gives you a massive, exceptionally full tone &#8211; perfect for high-energy solos, fast shred runs, and smooth, fusion-style legato playing. Total Control The Golden Jubilee was developed to function as a practical dual-drive platform in a single compact footprint, giving players direct control over two independent gain stages. Each channel operates with its own level, gain, and tone controls, making it easy to shape the signal without menu diving or guesswork. Three central toggles provide additional fine-tuning: two character switches that adjust the gain profile on the OD channel and the brightness of the DS channel, and an order switch that changes the stacking sequence of the drives. Gain and Versatility When you start dialing",
