      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.wamplerpedals.com/products/distortion-overdrive/mofetta/",
          "host": "www.wamplerpedals.com",
          "title": "Mofetta | Wampler Pedals",
          "h1": "Mofetta",
          "description": "The Mofetta is a smooth yet fiery overdrive / distortion pedal with MOSFET clipping for authentic tones.",
          "snippet": "Mofetta - Wampler Pedals",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Mofetta | Wampler Pedals Home Shop All Pedals Distortion / Overdrive Compression Fuzz Delay / Reverb Modulation Boost Utilities Discontinued Plugins Merchandise Dealers Community Blog Artists Podcast Videos Support About Downloads FAQs Warranty Registration Withdrawal Request Contact Us search account_circle My Account search Products search Mofetta The Mofetta is a smooth yet fiery overdrive / distortion pedal with MOSFET clipping for authentic tones. In stock Mofetta quantity Add to cart Watch video Overview Features Videos Technical Downloads In stock Mofetta quantity Add to cart &#8220;A Modern Twist on the &#8216;Mostortion&#8217; Pedal Circuitry&#8221; Right facing | Front | Left facing | Back | Top |' data-navmenu=\"off\" data-hashurl=\"off\" data-menuSlider=\"off\" data-continue-autoplay=\"off\" data-outside-nav=\"off\" data-autoplay=\"off\" > 4 5 The Wampler Mofetta Overdrive/Distortion is my tribute to the MOSFET-driven magic of a 1990s classic — the MT10 MOSTORTION tm . A mainstay of countless top session players, the Mofetta honors the soul of that elusive yet classic circuit while revealing its untapped potential. Think of the Mofetta as a supercharged MOSTORTION tm , reborn and amplified. I made sure that it delivered the classic, amp-like overdrive, massive headroom, and versatile 3-band EQ that made the original so famous. But I also wanted more and added a Texture Switch that introduces actual MOSFETs into the pedal's overdrive section for a bolder, more articulate tone. The Mofetta preserves everything you love about the early '90s legend with a powerful new dimension. The original MT10 MOSTORTION tm was released in 1990 as part of a budget pedal series to meet the demand of a growing market. Despite the pedal's \"cheaper\" qualities, guitarists began to take note of its amp-like low-gain tones, attributing them—arguably incorrectly—to the onboard MOSFET Op-amps. Though the pedals were discontinued a couple of years later, used ones command insane prices today and are extremely hard to find. The Mofetta is my way of bringing it all back and re-creating those singing tones while diving even further into the amp-like world of MOSFETs. The following designations are not owned by or associated with Wampler Pedals, Inc. but are instead owned by their respective owners: MT10 Mostortion, Mostortion &#36; 199.97 In stock Mofetta quantity Add to cart SKU: WMP-MFD-PED Category: Distortion / Overdrive Tags: distortion , MOSFET , overdrive warning Cancer and Reproductive Harm www.p65warnings.ca.gov Musical, Responsive Overdrive Paying tribute to a pedal called the MOSTORTION tm , it’s easy to assume the Mofetta would be a high-gain beast. But like its predecessor, it’s the circuit’s low-to-mid-gain voice that the original circuit is most known for. From edge-of-breakup to fat, vintage amp-style crunch, the Mofetta blooms with tube-like compression, always retaining its musical warmth. And with its high-headroom output, it easily pushes your amp or modeler into harmonically-rich breakup. 3-band EQ Part of what makes the Mofetta so versatile is its unique 3-band EQ. While many overdrives before 1990 relied on a simple tone knob, the idea of a dirt pedal like the MOSTORTION tm with bass, middle, and treble controls was darn near revolutionary. It lets you dial in the Mofetta for a full-range drive or achieve transparent grit that complements your clean tone. If you dial up the mids and treble a bit, you can even use it as a focused boost to push your amp’s breakup, or stacking with another gain pedal, tightening its response and enhancing its character. True MOSFET Clipping One of the original MOSTORTION’s tm little known “secrets” is that it doesn’t actually use MOSFETs for its overdrive. It uses a “MOSFET based op-amp”, but it uses clipping diodes to produce distortion. This left me thinking, “What if I built one that could actually use MOSFETs for the clipping, using multiple gain staging like a tube amp?” That’s what the Mofetta’s Te",
