          "bodyExcerpt": "Wampler Pedals TCD - The Compulsion Drive | Effects Database Skip to navigation Brands &#9660; 0-9... a... b... c... d... e... f... g... h... i... j... k... l... m... n... o... p... q... r... s... t... u... v... w... x... y... z... Effect types &#9660; boost distortion fuzz overdrive acoustic simulation amp simulation speaker/cabinet simulation chorus flanger phaser tremolo vibe vibrato other modulation pitch shifter octaver delay reverb looper/sampler hold/freeze eq filter wah fuzz-wah bitcrusher ring modulator samplerate reducer wavefolder synth effect granular effect multi effect vocal effect talkbox vocoder buffer compressor other... Countries &#9660; (country unknown) Argentina Australia Austria Belarus Belgium Brazil Bulgaria Canada Chile China Colombia Costa Rica Croatia Czech Republic Czechoslovakia DDR Denmark Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt Estonia Finland France Germany Greece Hungary India Indonesia Iran Ireland Israel Italy Japan Latvia Lithuania Luxembourg Macedonia Malaysia Malta Mexico Moldova Monaco Morocco Netherlands New-Zealand Norway Panama Peru Philippines Poland Portugal Romania Russia Serbia Singapore Slovakia Slovenia South-Africa South-Korea Spain Sweden Switzerland Taiwan Thailand Turkey U.K. U.S.A. U.S.S.R. Ukraine Uruguay Venezuela Browse by &#9660; Enclosure type Modulation type Special &#9658; Classics Eye candy Funny Vaporware Weird Random brand Random effect Events &#9658; NAMM Musikmesse Music China Guitar Summit More... &#9660; Forum (opens in new tab) myFXDB (opens in new tab) Newsletter About How to get listed? Interviews Reviews Effects explained Books D.I.Y. Schematics Links Contact Install Effects Database App Search the database browse by brand I... IndyGuitarist Wampler Pedals browse by type distortion/fuzz/overdrive overdrive browse by enclosure pedal Wampler Pedals TCD - The Compulsion Drive Published on November 28, 2025 Wampler Pedals overdrive pedal Information The Compulsion Drive (TCD) by Wampler Pedals is a high-performance overdrive and distortion pedal designed by Brian Wampler as a refined reinterpretation of one of the most iconic distortion circuits in modern guitar history. Built to capture the dynamic response, harmonic richness, and amp-like feel of the original design, The Compulsion Drive merges raw tonal aggression with sophisticated EQ control. Its circuit architecture allows for a wide range of gain textures, from articulate low-gain crunch to harmonically dense high-gain distortion, while retaining exceptional touch sensitivity and note definition. A key aspect of The Compulsion Drive is its dual personality, achieved through its selectable clipping modes and internal customization options. The external Mode switch toggles between a traditional gain structure and a more tube-like configuration featuring cascaded MOSFET gain stages, offering the player distinct flavors of compression and harmonic response. Internally, two DIP switches provide additional tonal tailoring: the Fat switch introduces added low-end warmth, while the Diode switch engages an extra clipping diode to produce a tighter, more saturated gain profile. These options allow the user to access four different circuit variations directly within the pedal without external modification. The Compulsion Drive incorporates a full three-band active EQ section with independent Bass, Mids, and Treble controls, offering precise tonal shaping beyond what is typical of most overdrive or distortion pedals. The Gain control spans from edge-of-breakup drive to fully saturated distortion, while the Level knob provides ample output to drive amplifiers or stack with other pedals. The result is a harmonically rich, amp-responsive distortion tool that adapts seamlessly to a variety of guitars and amplifiers. Constructed in the USA using high-grade components, The Compulsion Drive features a rugged, road-ready enclosure with a premium metallic finish. Its design emphasizes reliability, low noise, and long-term performan",
