          "bodyExcerpt": "Tweed &#039;57 Limited Edition | Wampler Pedals Home Shop All Pedals Distortion / Overdrive Compression Fuzz Delay / Reverb Modulation Boost Utilities Discontinued Plugins Merchandise Dealers Community Blog Artists Podcast Videos Support About Downloads FAQs Warranty Registration Withdrawal Request Contact Us search account_circle My Account search Products search Tweed &#8217;57 Limited Edition Bringing you classic tweed amp style tones that were at the very heart of Rock and Roll… Wampler’s Tweed ’57 pedal will help you create those iconic sounds you know and love! Out of stock Watch video Overview Features Videos Technical Downloads Out of stock &#8220;While the world moves increasingly toward digital modeling, these analog circuits offer something uniquely compelling.&#8221; Right facing | Front | Left facing | Back | Top |' data-navmenu=\"off\" data-hashurl=\"off\" data-menuSlider=\"off\" data-continue-autoplay=\"off\" data-outside-nav=\"off\" data-autoplay=\"off\" > 4 5 Coveted by blues, country, and rock players alike – tweed-style amplifiers have been staples in famous musicians’ live and studio setups since their introduction. With their warm and woolly sound and pushed volume tube break-up, the tone of tweed amps have found their way on to numerous historic recordings of some legendary artists such as Keith Richards, Eric Clapton, Neil Young, Billy Gibbons, and Joe Bonamassa. Those historic tweed-style amps and their legendary tones are responsible for the inspiration behind the Wampler Tweed ‘57. This pedal offers a wide tonal palette of sounds and includes several features that you’ve come to expect from Wampler. This is a limited edition pedal and only available to purchase online from Wamplerpedals.com. Once they’re gone, they’re gone! &#36; 199.97 Out of stock SKU: WMP-T57-PED Category: Distortion / Overdrive Tags: AIAB , Amp , Tweed warning Cancer and Reproductive Harm www.p65warnings.ca.gov Limited Edition, Classic Tones Although the Tweed ’57 delivers the sound of those vintage tones you have come to love and expect, it is not limited to only one specific “Tweed Amp” sound, instead it’s Brian’s take on the special topology and tones that amps like the classic Tweed deluxe, Bandmaster, and Bassman are known for. Iconic Sounds Whether you are playing a humbucker voiced guitar on a 60’s inspired rock song, or a slow single coils line in a classic blues number – Wampler’s Tweed ’57 pedal will help you create those iconic 50’s tweed sounds you have come to know and love – all at the click of a switch. Responsive Touch With a 3 band eq similar to a vintage tweed amp’s, you’re able to sculpt the tonality, feel, compression and overall gain structure just like you would on the real tube amplifier it’s emulating. Normal, Bright, and Linked input options cooperate with EQ and gain adjustments just like “jumpering inputs” on a vintage Bassman style amp. Amp in a Pedal Thanks to the fantastic “Input Simulator” switch, you will have flexibility and control just as you would expect on an amp from that period. All this in a compact pedal that works great with any amplifier or even direct into your favorite cabinet sim or IR loader. Hear it in action: Technical Details Limited Edition Built in the U.S.A. High-grade components selected for superior sound and response Controls: Volume, Gain, Bass, Middle and Treble, Input Selector Switch Unique input selector that reacts like the different inputs on the amps of this era 2.5″ x 4.5″ x 1.5″ in size (63.5mm x 114.3mm x 38.1mm) – height excludes knobs and switches Battery connection and 9V power jack Power draw: between 3mA (9V) and 9mA (18V) Classic tweed Bringing you classic tweed amp style tones that were at the very heart of Rock and Roll&#8230; Out of stock 5 Year Limited Warranty Each Wampler product that bears the official “Wampler – Built in USA” logo is custom designed and assembled in the USA using premium globally sourced components chosen for 