        {
          "url": "https://www.wamplerpedals.com/products/fuzz/velvet-fuzz/",
          "host": "www.wamplerpedals.com",
          "title": "Velvet Fuzz | Wampler Pedals",
          "h1": "Velvet Fuzz",
          "description": "",
          "snippet": "Velvet Fuzz - Wampler Pedals",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Velvet Fuzz | Wampler Pedals Home Shop All Pedals Distortion / Overdrive Compression Fuzz Delay / Reverb Modulation Boost Utilities Discontinued Plugins Merchandise Dealers Community Blog Artists Podcast Videos Support About Downloads FAQs Warranty Registration Withdrawal Request Contact Us search account_circle My Account search Products search Velvet Fuzz With all the character, power, and tone of a classic fuzz – the Velvet offers all this AND the option to tame the beast and bring it back under control. In stock Velvet Fuzz quantity Add to cart Watch video Overview Features Videos Technical Downloads In stock Velvet Fuzz quantity Add to cart &#8220;The key to the tone of the Velvet is the voicing switch. In the &#8220;big&#8221; position, the pedal reacts like a classic fuzz. In the &#8220;tight&#8221; position, the tone comes in fast!&#8221; Right facing | Front | Left facing | Back | Top |' data-navmenu=\"off\" data-hashurl=\"off\" data-menuSlider=\"off\" data-continue-autoplay=\"off\" data-outside-nav=\"off\" data-autoplay=\"off\" > 4 5 Looking back through history of great fuzz tone, there have been some truly outstanding examples - in particular, the tones that have been achieved by running a fuzz into a screaming stack. The kind of tones that are just earth shattering in their depth, aggression and smoothness. We took the base tones from a very famous Wampler Pedal (one that has the characteristics of a famous stacked, EL34 driven, amp) and decided this was the best foundation to build the perfect fuzz and deliver it in a unit that sounds as good as it feels powerful. With two completely different clipping options (not just the basic silicon or germanium option like most) you can achieve those classic fuzz big tones that compresses massively across the bottom or you can tighten them up and have it respond more like a distortion. With this you get all of the tone with none of the side effects. Some people say it sounds like a fuzz but feels like a distortion, so yes, you CAN have the best of both worlds. If you are a fan of the tones of the players like David Gilmour or Eric Johnson (and let’s face it, who isn’t), then it could be that the Velvet Fuzz is the pedal you are looking for. Welcome to a new world of thick as a brick, wall crumbling and window shattering fuzz. Velvet Fuzz. &#36; 199.97 In stock Velvet Fuzz quantity Add to cart SKU: WMP-VFZ-PED Category: Fuzz Tags: fuzz , velvet fuzz warning Cancer and Reproductive Harm www.p65warnings.ca.gov Not just another clone How many FF or BM clones are there out there? Lots… with the Velvet we wanted to bring you something different, we took a favorite circuit of ours and smashed the front end to bits to give an awesome full stack fuzz tone that will melt faces. Velvety Smooth The Velvet Fuzz is well known as been Velvety smooth… if screaming long notes are required, the Velvet lets you sing them on forever… You can bend a note, have a nap, and it’ll still be wailing by the time you wake up. Big or Tight Two clipping modes make the Velvet Fuzz one of the most versatile original fuzz circuits out there… One of them is gives you that beautifully horrible fat width, destroying the first three rows and the other is just sustain… smoothness and, yes, even more sustain. Built for Forever Brian Wampler’s attention to detail and commitment to bringing you the best-sounding most usable Effects Boxes on the market is nothing new. Those qualities are on full display within the Velvet Fuzz. We’re all tone-freaks, and we’re always trying new things, but we hope this pedal finds it’s forever home on your pedalboard, so we built it to last that long. Hear it in action: Technical Details Built in the U.S.A. High grade components picked for their superior sound and response Top mounted input and output jacks Battery connection and 9v power jack Power draw: 23mA (9v) ONLY (LED will flash 3 times when power from battery is getting low) Switchable between two completely independent clipping circuits",
