        {
          "url": "https://delicious-audio.com/way-huge-doom-hammer/",
          "host": "delicious-audio.com",
          "title": "Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz | Delicious Audio",
          "h1": "Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz",
          "description": "The Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz delivers thick saturation born from high-desert riffage and a &#039;90s sonic palette. Its lineage traces back to 1998, when designer Jeorge Tripps modified a late-&#039;70s op-amp fuzz circuit for the band Oranger. Prized for its less pronounced mid-scoop than many vintage fuzzes, the circuit was refined for tighter low-end response and reliable live performance.",
          "snippet": "Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz - Delicious Audio",
          "bodyExcerpt": "Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz | Delicious Audio Creative Pedals Creative Delay Tape Delay W/ Reverb Delay Distortion Fuzz Overdrive Dual Gain Dirt Boost Compr. + Dynamics Dynamics EQ Filter Wah Filter+EQ Lo-Fi 8 Bit Lo-fi Chorus Flanger Phaser Tremolo Uni-Vibe Modulation Pitch Shifter Octaver pitch Multiverb Reverb Spring Reverb Reverb CV In Granular Synth Pedals Synth Effect Guides Monthly Lists Shopping Guides Coverage Schedule Facebook Stompbox Exhibit Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz Updated Jun. 25, 2026 | by Paolo De Gregorio The Way Huge Doom Hammer Fuzz &#8216;s lineage traces back to 1998, when designer Jeorge Tripps modified a late-&#8217;70s op-amp fuzz circuit for the band Oranger. Prized for its less pronounced mid-scoop compared to many vintage fuzzes, the circuit was valued for its tighter low-end response and reliable live performance. Decades later, those prototypes evolved into the Doom Hammer. This new version retains the velvety harmonics of its predecessor but packs a more focused punch. The simple three-knob layout—Output, Tone, and Fuzz—offers wide-ranging control, from a delightful low-gain crunch to a dense wall of saturation. This makes it ideal for everything from gritty rock to modern doom, providing vintage character without losing definition. Housed in the compact Smalls enclosure, the Doom Hammer is a road-ready tribute to a cult-classic circuit, updated for today&#8217;s heavy tones. Related Delicious Audio Posts: Way Huge Stone Burner Sub Atomic Fuzz Way Huge Swollen Pickle Smalls MKIII Fuzz New Pedal: Way Huge Deep State Klon Clone Way Huge Geisha Drive Smalls Way Huge Attack Vector Updated Pedal: Cosmic Terror Sonic Doom V4 Fuzz Categories: Demos | FUZZ PEDALS Tags: Doom Hammer Fuzz | smalls | Way Huge Previous post Walrus Audio Highpoint Optical Compressor Next post New Pedal: Stonegate FX The Figure Filter Fuzz Post Your Comment Here Comment Name required Author Email required Email Website Search XHTML: You can us